Important subtlety: In POSIX shell, `local VAR=value` creates a *local variable*, which is NOT exported (unless the variable was previously exported in the environment). Subshells (command substitution) inherit a copy of the shell's variables including non-exported ones — actually, subshells in a POSIX shell inherit ALL shell variables (local and global), since fork() copies the whole shell state. Wait, that's true: a subshell is a fork of the shell, so it has all variables, including unexported ones. Only for `exec`'d commands (external commands) do only exported variables pass through.

